flang emits the standard F77 hidden-length ABI for CHARACTER dummy arguments:
one trailing size_t per CHARACTER*1 flag arg (TRANS/UPLO/DIAG/SIDE/JOBZ/...),
appended after all explicit args. scipy's hand-written C/C++ glue and every
vendored solver it bundles (SuperLU, PROPACK, the ARPACK "arnaud" C port)
declare and call the Fortran BLAS/LAPACK symbols WITHOUT those hidden lengths,
which is harmless where a lax C ABI ignores extra args but traps under wasm's
strictly typed call_indirect / dylib import (signature_mismatch:<sym>). scipy's
_batched_linalg additionally declares ?getrf/?getri as CBLAS_INT-returning
though flang's subroutines return void, a return-type mismatch under the same
strict typing. The f2py and cython_blas/cython_lapack paths already pass the
lengths (the latter via scipy-cython-blas-fortran-charlen.patch); this patch
brings every remaining hand-C declaration site to the same 15-arg-everywhere ABI.

For every affected routine each header now binds the true flang symbol to a
private C name via an asm label (carrying the hidden size_t lengths, and a void
return for the mis-declared ?getrf/?getri), defines a static inline wrapper
under a DISTINCT name that forwards and appends length 1 per char arg (every
wrapped arg is CHARACTER*1; LSAME reads only the first character, so the length
is always 1), and #(re)defines the public mangled name to the wrapper so
existing call sites bind to it with no edits. The wrapper must NOT reuse the true
symbol name: an asm label pointing at a same-named static inline makes the call
bind back to the wrapper, i.e. infinite self-recursion under wasm-ld. The whole
transform is gated on __wasi__/__wasm__, so non-wasm builds are unchanged.

Sites, by module: optimize _lbfgsb/_slsqp/nnls (optimize/src/blaslapack_
declarations.h); integrate _odepack/_vode (integrate/src/blaslapack_declarations.h);
linalg _internal_matfuncs expm/sqrtm (_common_array_utils.h) and _batched_linalg
(_common_array_utils.hh, incl. the getrf/getri return-type fix); sparse _superlu
(SuperLU/SRC/slu_[sdcz]defs.h, whose vendor-BLAS names are config-remapped, so
the redirect #undefs first); sparse _propack (PROPACK/src/include/blaslapack_
declarations.h); sparse arpack _arpacklib (arnaud/src/blaslapack_declarations.h,
ARNAUD_BLAS == BLAS_FUNC). Hidden-length counts and void returns were verified
against the flang-built reference lib arities (dgemm_ 15, dgemv_ 12, dgees_ 17,
dtrsyl_ 15, dtrevc_ 16, dgetri_ 7-void, ...).

The one remaining wasm-ld warning, cython_lapack chla_transtype_, is a CHARACTER-
RETURNING helper (a different hidden result-buffer ABI) that scipy never calls
directly; left as-is. Assumes the Fortran suffix is `_` (our reference build).
